Subject: collapsible: no permanent compositor layers

What: the collapsible arrow and its icon drop `will-change: opacity/transform`;
their 150 ms transitions promote a layer while they run.
Why: will-change on a stateless rule holds a compositor layer for every collapsible
on the page for as long as it is mounted.

diff --git a/src/components/collapsible.css b/src/components/collapsible.css
index 6ec4a71ded6436f36c80357c6258a59eca389033..eb78dca803410bc3dabce73196c8eeeb832ad9da 100644
--- a/src/components/collapsible.css
+++ b/src/components/collapsible.css
@@ -27,7 +27,6 @@
     .ui-collapsible-arrow {
       opacity: 0;
       transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
-      will-change: opacity;
       transform: translateZ(0);
     }
 
@@ -36,7 +35,6 @@
       color: var(--icon-weaker);
       transform: translateZ(0) rotate(-90deg);
       transition: transform 0.15s ease;
-      will-change: transform;
     }
 
     &:hover .ui-collapsible-arrow {
